{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused sinusoidal kernel is bit-for-bit identical to PyTorch across every tested batch, while saving about 9–14 µs. The custom SiLU is slightly less accurate and unexpectedly slower, so I’m dropping it. Before verification, I’m tuning only how the exact sinusoidal work is distributed across the GPU, especially for tiny batches."}}
